.TH QDRANT-MEMORY 1 "2026-11-26" "Homelab" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qdrant-memory \- reconcile the existing Nexus Qdrant knowledge collection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qdrant-memory.py status
.br
.B qdrant-memory.py sync-inbox [--dry-run] [--allow-empty]
.br
.B qdrant-memory.py sync-hermes [--dry-run] [--limit N]
.br
.B qdrant-memory.py sync-chat [--bootstrap | --dry-run] [--limit N]
.br
.B qdrant-memory.py sync-ops [--dry-run]
.br
.B qdrant-memory.py update TARGET [--dry-run]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The existing inbox and repository indexers use the same Qdrant collection and
Tensor Ollama embeddings. The separate
.B sync-hermes
command reads only completed default-profile Hermes compactions, applies
conservative item-level safety and provenance filters, then upserts
historically labelled records under
.BR origin=hermes_session .
It does not index full transcripts or modify other origins. The original inbox
command retains its previous semantics.
.B sync-chat
starts only after an explicit forward-only closed-session bootstrap (no historical
chat backfill). It reads default-profile CLI/TUI/Photon user and final-answer
pairs from a read-only SQLite snapshot only after durable explicit session close,
skipping compression, failed, open, other-profile, cron and delegated turns.
The session-close hook wakes the existing path unit; the hourly timer retries
missed events. It screens sensitive text before sending bounded
pairs to the existing Gemini 3.8 Flash High selector; accepted historical findings
are embedded with the existing Ollama model and stored separately as
.BR origin=hermes_chat .
Raw chats and model rejects are not exported or logged. No automatic deletion.
The
.B sync-ops
command uses the existing ops Markdown indexer on the Nexus checkout after
confirming its Markdown is committed. It skips uncommitted drafts and retries
on the next existing hourly service run. It does not fetch GitHub or index
private repository history. The indexer embeds only changed/new passages,
retains stale ops points for review, and confirms intended hashes after upsert.
The
.B --dry-run
mode performs no model calls or Qdrant writes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B QDRANT_MEMORY_INDEXERS
specifies the sibling script directory. In the Hermes container set
.B QDRANT_MEMORY_QDRANT=http://qdrant:6333
and
.B QDRANT_MEMORY_OPS=/opt/data/workspace/ops
and
.B QDRANT_MEMORY_STATE=/opt/data/state/qdrant-memory .
The database defaults to
.B /opt/data/state.db
and can be selected with
.BR QDRANT_MEMORY_HERMES_DB .
For the chat selector set
.B HOME=/opt/data
and
.B AGY_CLI_PATH=/opt/data/.local/bin/agy
only on the container's chat post-step. This selects the existing protected
Antigravity credential without copying or changing it. The installed
Antigravity plugin is required; Gemini output is validated before indexing.
.SH SECURITY
The database is read-only. The private checkpoint is mode 0600; the state
directory is mode 0700. The process lock rejects overlapping runs. Missing
Qdrant or Tensor Ollama leaves unconfirmed compactions for a later retry.
Only filtered, low-confidence historical findings are stored; validate
against authoritative Git and live state before applying them.
.SH FILES
.TP
/opt/data/state/qdrant-memory/hermes-compaction-checkpoint.json
Private per-compaction reconciliation state on the Hermes container.
.TP
/opt/data/state/qdrant-memory/hermes-chat-checkpoint.json
Private forward-only chat cursor and integrity digest; no transcript text.
.TP
shared/scripts/hermes_chat_memory.py
Read-only settled-turn scanner, privacy gate and isolated Gemini selector.
.TP
shared/scripts/hermes-compaction-export.py
Read-only source parser and conservative finding extractor.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qdrant-memory.service (5)
.PP
Full architecture, verification and scoped rollback:
.B docs/current/hermes-qdrant-memory.md
in public iragonforce/ops.
